---
title: Desktop control - consent, lease, serial input and native adapters (implemented)
---
classDiagram
  direction LR
  class DesktopService {
    platform: Arc dyn DesktopPlatform
    resources: Arc ResourceService
    artifacts: Arc ArtifactService
    store / clock / ids / authority
    git_source: Option Arc GitService
    desktop.inspect .capture (QueryHandler)
    desktop.request_control .input .release_control (CommandHandler)
    +approval_preview() +control_epoch() ControlEpoch
    +automation_may_be_active() bool
    +execute_input(op) InputEffectOutcome
    +observe_input(op) InputEffectOutcome
    +completion() typed input completion
  }
  class DesktopPlatform {
    <<trait>>
    +capabilities() DesktopCapabilities
    +capture_png() Vec u8
    +inject(DesktopInput)
    +accessibility_snapshot() default Unsupported
  }
  class DesktopCapabilities {
    target, capture, input, accessibility
    each Available, PermissionRequired or Unsupported
  }
  class AccessibilitySnapshot {
    platform, nodes, truncated
    +revision() sha256 digest
  }
  class DesktopInput {
    <<enum>>
    Click Text Key Scroll
    Target target_id, snapshot_revision, action
  }
  class DesktopTargetAction {
    <<enum>>
    Invoke SetValue Focus
  }
  class InputJob {
    frozen actor, project, root, fingerprint
    tested_repository, source_binding
    InputInput lease_id, expected_fence, consent_id
  }
  class ControlEpoch {
    grants and held
    +quiet_through(now)
  }
  class NativeDesktop {
    <<adapter>>
    enigo input, xcap capture
    capture and input are separate permissions
  }
  class AxMacos {
    <<adapter, macOS>>
    focused-app AX tree
    snapshot() inject_target()
  }
  class UiaWindows {
    <<adapter, Windows>>
    focused window via UI Automation
    snapshot() inject_target()
  }
  class AtspiLinux {
    <<adapter, Linux>>
    session AT-SPI bus
    snapshot() inject_target()
  }
  class ResourceService {
    machine resource desktop
    acquire_desktop() authorize_dispatch()
  }
  class InputEffects {
    <<engine consumer desktop_input_effects>>
    max_in_flight 1, max_attempts 1
    execute and observe
  }
  class DesktopComposition {
    <<engine config>>
    platform: Arc dyn DesktopPlatform
  }
  class OwnerPreview {
    <<approvals>>
    desktop.request_control consent
  }
  class Runtime {
    <<engine>>
    desktop_control_epoch()
    record_human_decision_received and confirm_project_purge_received
  }
  DesktopService o-- DesktopPlatform
  DesktopService o-- ResourceService
  DesktopService ..> InputJob : frozen as operation payload
  DesktopService ..> ControlEpoch : reads the desktop lease state
  DesktopPlatform ..> DesktopCapabilities
  DesktopPlatform ..> AccessibilitySnapshot
  DesktopPlatform ..> DesktopInput
  DesktopInput *-- DesktopTargetAction
  NativeDesktop ..|> DesktopPlatform
  NativeDesktop ..> AxMacos : target_os macos
  NativeDesktop ..> UiaWindows : target_os windows
  NativeDesktop ..> AtspiLinux : target_os linux
  DesktopComposition o-- DesktopPlatform : host default is NativeDesktop
  InputEffects o-- DesktopService
  OwnerPreview o-- DesktopService
  Runtime ..> ControlEpoch : trusted human confirmations need it quiet
  note for NativeDesktop "macOS and Windows capture with xcap. Linux X11 captures natively. Wayland reports capture and input Unsupported and accessibility still uses AT-SPI. Each OS module is built only on its own target by cfg"
  note for DesktopService "Not built: a Wayland portal input session. Accessibility snapshots read the focused app or window only"
